WEBVTT

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:37.090
Kou Shuurei has become a joukan,
but she has no time to worry about herself.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:46.300
To ensure that other joukan aren't dismissed, she urges them, over and over, to get a job.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.500
F-Finished...

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.140
Thanks for the hard work.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.900
The day's already over?

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.550
I told you, "Don't spend too much time on others."

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:25.950
Stop worrying about everything and everyone, especially men.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.460
I'm not worrying about everything and everyone.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.610
That's according to your standards.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.710
According to mine, it's everything and everyone.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.270
I think this level of help is fine.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.410
She's only wasted one day.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.890
Stop spoiling her.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.060
Anyway, what are you going to do for yourself, Seiga-kun?

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.470
You've spent the whole day with us.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:50.350
I know where I'm going, so I don't have a problem.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.180
Eh?

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:52.350
When did you manage that?

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.850
During the breaks,

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:56.690
I asked my supervisor about it.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.200
You know how to get on the world, don't you?

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.830
So I'm told.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.360
So there are people like that.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.820
They do what's necessary, but don't put in too much effort.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.210
The complete opposite of me.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.640
How old are you, Seiga-san?

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.750
I'll turn twenty this year.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.630
He's only two years older than me.
Where does that sense of calm come from?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:27.070
Seriously, you two are so young, but all you think about is work, work, career, career.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:27.970
What's up with you guys?

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.040
Huh?

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.430
I'm sure there's more to life than that.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:36.590
When a young man and woman of marriageable age meet, shouldn't their hearts flutter?

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.840
Isn't that what's normal?

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.560
Suou-kun, how can you say that?

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:47.140
It looks as though those two will become worthy rivals.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:51.460
Why do you want to turn them into something else?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.230
Worthy rivals?

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.830
Seiga-san, are you out to make a career?

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.130
Yes.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.630
Is there someone you look up to?

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:05.890
Umm... no, I am who I am, so I don't think I need to look up to anyone.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.930
Does that mean he thinks he's the best?

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.160
Probably.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.150
Really, it's amazing how he doesn't make it sound arrogant.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.150
No, I don't mean it like that.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.770
How should I say this?

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:24.650
I decided I wanted to go as far as I could on my own.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:28.590
Great... Here we have another splendid Mr. Very-Able-Candidate.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.970
I feel so small.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.200
Tan-tan, stop saying everything that pops into your head!

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.960
Speaking of that, what are you going to do, Tan-tan?

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.960
Well, I have a plan too, so I'm okay.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.890
I-Is that so?

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.240
Are you sure you're going to be okay?

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.530
Probably.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.470
If you say so...

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.210
What about you, Shuurei-san?

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.970
Is there a particular department you want to be in?

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.890
The Civil Service, the Departments of Finance and Education...

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:11.960
If I beg them, there are places that will give me a job.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:23.170
But, until the last moment, I should work under the same conditions as the other joukan.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.260
I'll give it some thought.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.000
Really, don't aim too high.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.660
Just take a position where you can do okay without having to work too hard.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:39.480
Tan-tan, you never say, "Go for it!" or "Try hard!", do you?

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:43.070
You'd work hard even if I didn't say it, wouldn't you?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.490
I'm just telling you not to put all that effort in the wrong place.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:53.240
Oh, by the way, rice balls...

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.780
Rice balls?

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.560
I just can't get the taste and shape of them right.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.740
Do you mind teaching me how to make them?

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.750
No, I don't mind.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.140
Can I send him some food?

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.940
You've come again?

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.140
It's good of you to come by every day.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.410
Dad, it's me.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.740
Are you still alive?

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:32.740
Suou...

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.000
Some food for you.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:44.960
Bamboo leaf rice again?

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.340
They're rice balls!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.920
They've just lost their shape.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.220
I'm learning how to make them, so eventually I'll treat you to proper rice balls.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.730
Dad...

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.680
I'm sorry.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:09.240
No, I was the stupid one.

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:13.240
You're my dad. You couldn't help it.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:18.750
Did you think Mom would come back if you earned money and impressed others with it?

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.450
Did you want her to come back that badly?

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:28.630
After all, she had an affair with another man, took your money, and left you.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.120
I'm sorry.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:33.060
It's okay.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:35.350
We're both stupid anyway.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.010
Hey, Dad...

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:43.870
When you get out of here, let's go to the country.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:48.020
I think we're better suited to being commoners than nobles.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:57.160
It's salty. I can taste sandy salt.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.800
Well, I'll come by again, Dad.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.620
Suou...

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:13.350
I'm glad you were the first person to catch me.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:18.720
I... wanted to tell you to live life as you like. Don't worry about me.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.370
Thanks, Dad.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.610
Make it quick.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.210
It's futile to ask me to spare your father's life.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:48.790
Won't you even listen to what I've got to offer you?

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:52.170
Well, tell me.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.490
I have a report from an undercover official about Shuurei.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.220
Kou Shuurei is too soft-hearted.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:08.240
With her current temperament,
she'll be useless in the central government.

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:11.730
However, as an official in a rural area,

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.840
she has the potential to be moderately successful.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.860
Find him at night and smack his stupid face two or three times!

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.790
He's as rude as ever!

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:29.670
He won't back down just because he gets smacked, and his judgment is accurate.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:32.820
I don't like it because it's too accurate!

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:37.880
Then you also think Shuurei will fail
if she remains as she is now?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:46.770
That's for Shuurei to decide, not me.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:51.320
I'm happy as long as she does well.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:53.280
I don't wish for anything else.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.580
It's all up to Shuurei herself to decide.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:58.280
Yes.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:09.040
Huh? The texture isn't right.

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.030
The salt is grainy.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:17.420
Did I buy the cheapest salt by mistake?

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:21.930
I'm home, oujo-sama.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.820
Oh, welcome home, Seiran.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:26.930
I've brought some dumplings home.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:31.120
Wow, those are pretty famous dumplings! Thank you.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:39.570
S-Seiran, those books...

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:43.710
Oh, would oujo-sama like to read them too?

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.720
They're about war tactics.

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.580
Oh, about war tactics, right...

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:52.090
Even your super-handsome family retainer...

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:57.090
is bound to have a book like this hidden under the bed or at the bottom of his closet.{ep23}

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:00.270
Umm, oujo-sama, is something wrong?

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:05.900
Hey Seiran, would you mind if I looked under your bed and at the bottom of your closet?

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:08.480
Huh? No, not at all,

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.150
but why do you want to look there?

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:13.020
I don't have any secret savings.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.280
Oh no, in that case, it's all right.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:17.240
Please don't worry about it.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:22.280
You're having doubts about me, aren't you?

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.020
Please don't worry.

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.960
It really was nothing.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:28.080
Umm...

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.520
Well, Tan-tan said...

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:40.760
Tan-tan-kun?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:46.920
He said that you're also a man, so you're bound to have secret stuff like peach-colored books,

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.260
so I was a little concerned...

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:49.150
Well...

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:52.340
No, it's okay! You're a man, after all. That's normal, right?

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:55.020
Even if I find them by accident, I'll pretend I didn't see them, rest assured!

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:59.190
You can search wherever you like, but you won't find any.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:02.030
If I had money for that, I'd give it to you for food.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.470
I-I thought so! I'm sorry.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:08.420
It's okay, as long as you understood.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:14.690
But... you knew what peach-colored books were, Seiran.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:27.930
Right. Tan-tan-kun will feel a taste of hell tomorrow.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:42.180
Shuurei, how does it feel to work after so long?

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:44.210
You think you'll manage all right?

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:46.780
I-I'll manage it somehow.

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:50.340
What's wrong? Is something bothering you?

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:58.310
It's more like I envy this man, like I'm jealous...

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:01.550
Oh, so you've found yourself a rival?

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:06.550
A rival? But I only met him today.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:08.890
I hardly know him.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:17.560
Ensei told me many times to learn to relax, but I just can't do it.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:20.240
I always wind up running at full speed.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:27.380
But this person knows when to relax and how to manage matters calmly.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.820
I just feel a bit uneasy about it.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:33.450
Well, that's what it's like to have a rival.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:35.670
Really?

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:43.140
A person who has something you don't,
something you may never acquire, even if you try.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:48.220
It's as if you're on opposite poles, particularly if you're close in age.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:56.590
Sometimes they turn into lifetime enemies, though.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:02.010
A rival... I wonder.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.650
Is he also a joukan?

00:14:05.180 --> 00:14:07.690
I'm not actually sure.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:11.570
He doesn't seem like he's about to be fired.

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:19.830
So, what are you going to do starting tomorrow?

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:23.340
Work hard, of course!

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.900
What? What's going on?!

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:36.380
They've come back because they were rejected at the door.

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:39.640
What? But of course they'd get rejected at first!

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.730
Somehow they have to beg...

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:48.150
Come on, if they had that much energy and will power, they wouldn't be joukan in the first place.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.870
Very well, I'll listen to what each of you has to say.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.380
Huh? What do you mean?

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.910
I've got to shout and push them out one by one.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.010
That's not what I asked.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:01.660
I'm telling you, just leave them alone.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:03.160
Could you just leave them?!

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:04.380
Sure I could!

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.250
It's none of your business.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.880
"None of my business"?

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:09.760
I don't like that phrase.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.040
Can you do it?

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:16.390
Do something about these guys and sort yourself out as well?

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.140
I'll show you.

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:22.150
I got it. I won't interfere anymore.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:26.170
Why don't you get Seiga-kun to help give them talks about trying their best?

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.400
I'll help you.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:33.420
This really is a dreadful sight.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:39.160
Well, if you work with Seiga-kun, there's a chance you might just make it somehow.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.660
Good for you.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.710
Tan-tan, you're going?

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:50.210
Of course. Unlike Seiga-kun, I haven't got a job yet, nor do I have contacts like you.

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:53.840
If I just sit around, then I'll be dismissed in no time.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:56.460
Y-You're right.

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:03.210
It's not like I dislike your soft-heartedness, so why not give it your best shot?

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:07.230
If you think you can't make it,
then just give up whenever it suits you.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.810
I'll recommend a saying to you, "Giving up is essential."

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:19.520
Seiga-san, please help me.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:22.980
We'll get everyone out of this room and into a job!

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:31.800
Tan-tan-kun?

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:37.350
The family retainer with the bamboo shoots!

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.520
Huh? Did you say something?

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.100
N-No, nothing.

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:46.060
By the way, you said something
unnecessary to oujo-sama, didn't you?

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:51.860
Don't tell me... she found your peach-colored books?

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:54.320
Or something more advanced?

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:56.960
I don't have either.

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:02.450
Hey, you're too over-protective about her!

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:08.050
Aren't you, and no one else, responsible for her complete inability to sense danger?

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:12.320
Also, why don't you teach her a few more lessons?

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.490
Like if she runs too much, she'll fall over one day?

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:18.710
You don't seem to be thinking enough about that sort of stuff.

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:23.100
Tan-tan-kun, you've got keener eyes than I thought.

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:27.600
It might do oujo-sama good to have you around.

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:32.360
Anyway, if you don't have any business with me, can I go?

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:39.120
Oh, I know you probably can't help,
but can I ask a favor of you, just in case?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.630
A favor of me?

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:41.640
What is it?

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:47.890
Well...

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:09.870
If you give up now, your life as a man will be over.

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:11.760
What?! No...

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:17.040
But if you try hard now, I think your life won't be so bad.

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:20.950
Y-You think? Right, I'll do it!

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:23.890
Right, next!

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:29.860
Well, they seem to do well together, don't they?

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:34.530
Yes, Suou-san, they make a perfect pair. It's amazing.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.910
So? How are they doing?

00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:40.470
They're pushing them out one by one like that.

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:46.470
But some come back again, so it's endless.

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:49.500
I thought so.

00:18:57.950 --> 00:18:59.330
So, how was it?

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:02.870
Have you considered giving up yet?

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:04.720
Tan-tan, what's the matter with you?

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:07.520
You're the one who said, "I don't dislike it, so give it your best."

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:09.900
But I didn't say I liked it.

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:16.750
Anyway, I made rice balls the way you taught me, so here's one for you.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.190
Thank you.

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.380
It has quite a good shape, doesn't it?

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:23.450
Yes, but it's huge.

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:26.570
Thanks all the same. I was just getting hungry.

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:28.130
Thanks for the meal.

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:36.270
The salt texture isn't the best, but it tastes great, Tan-tan!

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:40.110
Well, why don't you do a bit more work after you eat the rice ball?

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.150
What? Working hours are over.

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:46.120
Don't tell me...

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:50.860
Those guys' personalities won't improve that easily.

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:02.280
What is it? You came to bring him food again?

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:03.340
Again?

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:05.990
You dropped some food off at lunch time, too.

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:07.600
You really take care of him well.

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:13.600
Aren't I a good son?

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.980
Yeah, you are.

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:21.070
Hey, you're supposed to laugh here, not get sympathetic.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.240
Dad...

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:38.440
I'm finally done, but it's already late.

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:41.840
Am I really going to be able to sort something out by the deadline?

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:48.680
Good evening, lady.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:51.930
Umm, yes, g-good evening...

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:53.830
Have this peach.

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:56.460
You did well, working so hard today.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.810
That's for you.

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.260
Well, umm, I'm sorry to be rude, but who are you?

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:02.450
Anjuu.

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:05.820
It'd be great if you'd peel it for me.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.660
I like peaches, but they're not easy to eat.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.750
A-A peach wizard?!

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:20.840
You're good at it.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.680
Y-Yeah...

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:30.300
Hmm, this tastes great.

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:35.070
Do you think if you work hard, you won't be dismissed?

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:39.060
I don't think I won't, I'm going to make sure I won't.

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:40.820
Is that so?

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.570
I wish you good luck.

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:55.430
I find it tastes best if someone feeds me like this.

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:57.790
Well then, take care and have a safe journey home.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:12.560
My...

00:22:16.300 --> 00:22:18.500
It's unusual to find you here.

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:21.060
Is what you've told me true?

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:26.880
Ah, that the girl is trying to do something about the other joukan too?

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:28.570
Yes, it's true.

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:31.570
She disgusts me.

00:22:31.810 --> 00:22:35.050
She's hard-working, honest, and cute, you know.

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:38.820
I can't believe that she's Kou Reishin's niece.

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:43.340
When I asked her, she peeled the peach neatly and fed it to me.

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:44.830
A peach, huh?

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:50.170
She's the kind of girl I want to smash like a peach and cast down as far as possible.

00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:05.950
There's... someone here.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:16.540
Who's there?

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:28.050
Are you... Shi Ryuuki?

00:24:45.350 --> 00:24:48.400
Only half a month left until we're fired.

00:24:48.400 --> 00:24:51.760
Should I just beg and get a job no matter where?

00:24:52.220 --> 00:24:54.750
But is it really fair to do this?

00:24:54.750 --> 00:24:57.290
What am I supposed to do?!
